### Guide §5.7 Security. VS Code REST Client syntax: click "Send Request" above each request.
### Start the app with the dev profile (demo users, all with the password "demo-password"):
###   ./mvnw -pl spring-app spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=dev
### Ids and statuses assume the demo data on an empty database, and a first run of this file: reset
### with docker compose -f spring-app/compose.yaml down -v
### Demo ids: members Ada 1, Alan 2, Grace 3, the librarian 4; loan 3 is Alan's copy of The Dispossessed.
### "# @name x" names a request; {{x.response.body.accessToken}} reuses its token.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### No token (401): a ProblemDetail, and "WWW-Authenticate: Bearer" says how to authenticate
GET {{host}}/api/books

### The API itself is public (200)
GET {{host}}/api/info

### Log in as the librarian (200): {"accessToken": "eyJ...", "tokenType": "Bearer", "expiresIn": 3600}.
### Paste the accessToken into https://jwt.io to read its claims: signed, not encrypted
# @name librarian
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "librarian@library.test", "password": "demo-password"}

### A librarian changes the catalogue (201)
POST {{host}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780547928227", "title": "The Hobbit", "publishedYear": 1937, "totalCopies": 1}

### Log in as Ada, a member (200). The email is case-insensitive
# @name ada
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "Ada@Library.test", "password": "demo-password"}

### Who am I (200: Ada, role MEMBER). The token's subject is the member id
GET {{host}}/api/members/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ada.response.body.accessToken}}

### Ada borrows Cosmos for herself (201, memberId 1): no memberId in the body, it comes from the token
# @name loan
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{ada.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 8}

### Ada's own loans (200: Dune and Cosmos, and the returned Emma)
GET {{host}}/api/members/me/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{ada.response.body.accessToken}}

### Ada returns her loan (200): she owns it
POST {{host}}/api/loans/{{loan.response.body.id}}/return
Authorization: Bearer {{ada.response.body.accessToken}}

### A member cannot change the catalogue (403, a URL rule)
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/1
Authorization: Bearer {{ada.response.body.accessToken}}

### ...nor list everyone's loans (403, a URL rule)
GET {{host}}/api/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{ada.response.body.accessToken}}

### ...nor read Alan's loan (403, @PreAuthorize on LoanService.findById)
GET {{host}}/api/loans/3
Authorization: Bearer {{ada.response.body.accessToken}}

### ...nor borrow in Alan's name (403)
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{ada.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 8, "memberId": 2}

### A librarian may borrow on a member's behalf (201, memberId 2)
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 8, "memberId": 2}

### The audit trail is for librarians: Ada gets a 403...
GET {{host}}/api/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{ada.response.body.accessToken}}

### ...the librarian a 200
GET {{host}}/api/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}

### A token with one character added to its signature (401, error="invalid_token")
GET {{host}}/api/members/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ada.response.body.accessToken}}x

### A wrong password (401, "Invalid email or password."): the same answer as for an unknown email
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "ada@library.test", "password": "not-the-password"}

### Register a new member (201, role MEMBER, Location /api/members/5). The console shows the insert
### with the password as a {bcrypt} hash
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "katherine@library.test", "fullName": "Katherine Johnson", "password": "orbital-mechanics"}

### A password below 8 characters (400, errors.password)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "dorothy@library.test", "fullName": "Dorothy Vaughan", "password": "fortran"}

### A CORS preflight from the Angular dev server (200, Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:4200).
### A browser sends it by itself before a cross-origin POST with a JSON body
OPTIONS {{host}}/api/books
Origin: http://localhost:4200
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization, content-type

### The same preflight from another origin (403, "Invalid CORS request")
OPTIONS {{host}}/api/books
Origin: https://evil.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
